==Strategy==
The idea here is to use the starting enemies to get money, then spawn your attackers to kill Kiss and Koi. Keep in mind that it is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating enemy]] and that it has 400 range, meaning that even [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] gets outranged. Instead, use units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], or any long ranged [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] to kill it. Rushers like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and Awakened Bahamut Cat also work here to deal a lot of damage to the boss. Once you kill the boss, kill any remaining enemies left and you're free to destroy the enemy base.

You can cheese this stage by spawning Can Can Cat to make some money along with some Crazed Wall Cats to protect him. Afterwards, send out Awakened Bahamut Cat when you have enough money and he will destroy the base before any major threat comes out.

==Trivia==
*The name of this stage is a reference to the phrase ''carpe diem'', which in Latin means "seize the day".

